# Related Work

RFC Editor: please remove this appendix before publication.

Other documents under discussion cover parts of the same ground:

* {{I-D.fengfar-led}} discusses the use of AI tools in IETF mailing
  list discussions and recommends that the IETF develop guidelines for
  them.  It notes that the sock-puppet problem is a separate issue.
  This document addresses that issue.

* {{I-D.carpenter-rswg-authoring-ethics}} states that authors remain
  entirely responsible for any content generated by AI, and that an AI
  tool must not be credited as an author.  This document applies the
  same principle to every Contribution, not only to RFC authorship.

* {{I-D.moonesamy-authorship-ietf}} reflects on authorship in the IETF
  and asks whether the IETF should set guidelines for the use of
  generative AI by authors.

Some documents cited here are being revised.  {{I-D.ietf-procon-2418bis}}
would replace {{RFC2418}} and keeps the text quoted in
{{existing-principle}}.  {{I-D.ietf-procon-2026bis}} would replace
{{RFC2026}}.  References will be updated if those documents are
published first.

